ext":"Send Back","secondTabOffset":80,"secondTabWidth":65},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":102,"type":"PrimitiveNode","pos":[-140,-290],"size":[268.3984375,82],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"INT","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"seed"},"links":[257,258]}],"title":"seed","properties":{"Run widget replace on values":false},"widgets_values":[908275943238648,"randomize"]},{"id":105,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1180,-710],"size":[480,560],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## ACE-Step 1.5 -- MP3 Retake / Variation\n\nTurns an existing instrumental MP3 into a new variation that keeps its\noverall structure, rhythm and tonality, guided by a text prompt -- the\nComfyUI equivalent of Suno's \"create variation from audio\".\n\n### How it works\n`LoadAudio` -> `VAEEncodeAudio` encodes your MP3 into the ACE-Step 1.5\nlatent space, replacing the usual empty/silent starting latent. `KSampler`\nthen only partially re-noises/denoises it (see `denoise` below) instead of\ngenerating from scratch, so the result stays close to the source.\n\n### Exploring variations (added 2026-08-16)\n`RepeatLatentBatch` (amount=4) now sits between `VAEEncodeAudio` and\n`KSampler`: one Queue run renders 4 takes at once (each gets different noise\neven with a single seed), and `SaveAudioMP3` saves all 4 -- same idea as\nSuno's grid of options, listen and pick. Raise/lower `amount` for\nmore/fewer takes per run (more = more VRAM/time).\n\n`denoise` is now `0.6` (was `0.4`) -- 0.4 stayed too close to a near-exact\ncopy (same structure, same everything). 0.55-0.7 is usually the zone where\nthe piece still feels like the same song (rhythm/tonal character carries\nover) but the piano phrasing genuinely reinterprets itself instead of\njust re-rendering. Denoise is a single global knob -- it can't isolate\n\"keep the beat, vary the melody\" on its own, so nudge it and re-listen;\ntags now also explicitly ask for melodic variation that reprises the\nrecurring piano motif.\n\n### Steps to use it\n1. Click the `LoadAudio` node (\"Load Your MP3 (input to vary)\") and upload\n   your MP3.\n2. Set `bpm`, `duration` (seconds) and `keyscale` on the text-encode node to\n   roughly match your source track for best coherence.\n3. Write what you want changed/emphasized in `tags` (already has a starting\n   instrumental/piano prompt -- edit it). `lyrics` stays `[instrumental]`\n   since there's no vocal.\n4. Tune `KSampler.denoise` (currently `0.4`):\n   - lower (0.2-0.3) = closer to the original, subtle variation\n   - higher (0.5-0.7) = more creative freedom, less faithful to the source\n   Run it a few times with different seeds/denoise until you get a take you like,\n   same idea as Suno.\n\n### Model\n- [ace_step_1.5_turbo_aio.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/ace_step_1.5_ComfyUI_files/resolve/main/checkpoints/ace_step_1.5_turbo_aio.safetensors)\n  -> `models/checkpoints/`. Download via `mauro-files/download-ace-step.sh`.\n\n### Note\nThis is a manually adapted workflow -- ComfyUI's official ACE-Step 1.5\ntemplates only ship text-to-audio (from-scratch) examples, no img2img/retake\none yet. The `turbo` checkpoint is distilled for an 8-step full schedule, so\npartial-denoise quality at very low `denoise` may be inconsistent -- if a\ntake sounds muddy, try raising `steps` and/or `denoise` a bit.\n"],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":106,"type":"LoadAudio","pos":[-680,-270],"size":[320,136],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"audio","name":"audio","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"audio"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"audioUI","name":"audioUI","type":"AUDIO_UI","widget":{"name":"audioUI"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"choose file to upload","name":"upload","type":"AUDIOUPLOAD","widget":{"name":"upload"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"AUDIO","name":"AUDIO","type":"AUDIO","links":[262]}],"title":"Load Your MP3 (input to vary)","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.11.1","Node name for S&R":"LoadAudio"},"widgets_values":["Enkidu - Falling (Lambert Rework) [a3SRbaRdjmI].mp3",null,null]},{"id":107,"type":"VAEEncodeAudio","pos":[-331.2049889894225,-153.23222000496528],"size":[270,60],"flags":{},"order":8,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"audio","name":"audio","type":"AUDIO","link":262},{"localized_name":"vae","name":"vae","type":"VAE","link":261}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"LATENT","name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[263]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.11.1","Node name for S&R":"VAEEncodeAudio"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":109,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[70.10142761496773,-1134.0403335089159],"size":[553.722490191567,231.2351417737318],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["slow tempo, piano, warm and intimate, gentle sustain, soft dynamics, ambient pad undertones, cinematic, relaxing, instrumental, no vocals, melodic variation, reprising the same recurring piano motif/hook, same steady rhythmic pulse and background ambience, a few new embellishments"],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":94,"type":"TextEncodeAceStepAudio1.5","pos":[270.09895833333337,-670],"size":[611.9140625,569.7526041666667],"flags":{},"order":7,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"clip","name":"clip","type":"CLIP","link":244},{"localized_name":"tags","name":"tags","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"tags"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"lyrics","name":"lyrics","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"lyrics"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"seed","name":"seed","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"seed"},"link":257},{"localized_name":"bpm","name":"bpm","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"bpm"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"duration","name":"duration","type":"FLOAT","widget":{"name":"duration"},"link":251},{"localized_name":"timesignature","name":"timesignature","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"timesignature"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"language","name":"language","ty